questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue where a Spring Boot microservice periodically crashes with `java.lang.OutOfMemoryError: Metaspace` after running for several days in production. The application dynamically compiles and executes custom business logic scripts submitted by users. You inspect the following code snippet from the rule processing service:

java
@Service
public class DynamicRuleEngine {
    @Autowired
    private AutowireCapableBeanFactory beanFactory;

    public void executeCustomRule(String ruleName, byte[] classBytes) throws Exception {
        CustomClassLoader loader = new CustomClassLoader(getClass().getClassLoader());
        Class<?> ruleClass = loader.defineClass(ruleName, classBytes);
        Object ruleInstance = ruleClass.getDeclaredConstructor().newInstance();
        beanFactory.autowireBean(ruleInstance);
        ((Runnable) ruleInstance).run();
    }
}

You are debugging a production issue where a high-throughput multi-threaded Spring component fails to shut down gracefully. Worker threads running a processing loop fail to acknowledge a state update performed by an administrative endpoint thread. You review the following implementation:

java
@Component
public class WorkerTaskProcessor {
    private boolean active = true;

    public void shutdown() {
        this.active = false;
    }

    public void processLoop() {
        while (active) {
            // Perform non-blocking processing task
        }
    }
}
